# Proper server-side 301s (Cloudflare) — replaces Astro's static meta-refresh
# pages so social scrapers and search engines follow them. Destinations carry
# the trailing slash to match the canonical URLs (avoids an extra hop).
# Format rename (Jul 2026): beats → play, reads → read, dashboards → explore.
# Splats carry deep links (old shared article/deck/dashboard URLs) across.
# /economy points straight at the read shelf — never chain through /reads.
# Retired formats send old URLs to a LISTED page, not to the unlisted survivor
# (revised Jul 2026): /economy/beats was the site's most-indexed URL, and
# pointing it at the retired payments deck walked every search visitor onto a
# noindex page with nothing after it. Beats goes to the front page; retired
# short reads go to the shelf. Both destinations are live surfaces a reader can
# continue from. The pages themselves stay served — unlisted, not unpublished.
/economy/beats/*        /                        301
/economy/beats          /                        301
/economy/beats/         /                        301
# Only the longread keeps its own destination; the retired shorts land on the
# shelf. EVERY slug is spelled out and there is deliberately no /economy/reads/*
# splat: on Cloudflare a splat beats an exact rule that also matches, whatever
# the file order (verified on prod — `wrangler dev` honours order, prod does
# not), so a surviving slug can never be listed alongside a splat that would
# swallow it. /economy/reads/upi-architecture is the old URL of the most-read
# page and the one the HN post links to; it must reach the piece, not the shelf.
# The list is closed — these nine are every read that ever shipped on the old
# scheme — so nothing new can arrive here needing a fallback.
